for this round; once this comment posts, it is removed again (node_modules first, git worktree remove without --force).",
  "tests": "All at 49804f28cf (git rev-parse --short HEAD after the last commit). Each exit code was captured by redirect-then-capture, before any pipe. node scripts/pm/fleet-write/validate.mjs --self-test: exit 0, '193 cases pass across 12 batteries'. The run_rerun_failed battery's pin rose 30 to 33, with three new head cases: a stale head, an answer for another pull, a missing head_sha and no pull answer each refused naming the head fence alone; the embedded copy agreeing with head_sha while the pull's own answer moved on, refused; a run naming no pull (empty, absent, no number) refused by name. The measured-run acceptance now requires the pull's current head, and every-fence-in-one-pass now names 5. node scripts/pm/fleet-write/execute.mjs --self-test: exit 0, '188 cases pass across 19 batteries'. Its pin rose 17 to 21. The happy path reads PERM, attempt 1 jobs, the run, the pull, then the POST. Four new cases: a stale head refused with zero writes, the pull read the last request and both heads named; the embedded copy never trusted; a fork run (pull_requests empty or absent) refused with zero writes and NO pull read; an unreadable pull with zero writes. The four older fence refusals now end on the pull read. node scripts/pm/fleet-write/dispatch.mjs --self-test: exit 0, '247 cases pass across 22 batteries', unchanged (Q4 A); its conformance drives the wrapper's probe through the new pull read. node scripts/pm/rerun-failed.mjs --self-test: exit 0, '31 cases pass across 5 batteries'. The seat-fence battery pin rose 8 to 11: a stale head refused (exit 2, no dispatch), a fork run refused by name with no pull read, and an unreadable pull exit 3; accepted reads the run, then the pull, then attempt 1. pnpm check:pm-fleet-write-dispatch now prints both success lines, exit 0. One defect was caught in development: three validator cases first failed (3 of 193) because they passed the fence helper to Array.map, whose index landed in the new pull parameter. The helper was split into a one-argument fenced and a two-argument fencedWith, and the run is green. Ablation: none, because the diff is scripts and one npm script line.",
  "gates": "Local, at 49804f28cf. node scripts/pm/dispatch-gates.mjs --commands --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack: exit 0. Its first line names objectstack-ai/objectstack at 49804f28cf; the change set is 7 paths vs merge base 6251f5905, 1408 changed lines under 3000. It derived 59 commands (51 before; package.json adds check-dts-emitted --self-test, dts-closure, dual-build-cjs-loads, lean-entry-closure, manifest-repository-directory, merge-driver, sourcemap-no-sources-content and turbo-task-graph). pnpm check:pm-dispatch-gates ran detached under nohup and was waited out: EXIT_CODE=0, fast tier, 290.8s. Of the other 58, 53 exited 0 at once. Five exited 3, PREREQUISITE NOT MET, on the fresh worktree, which are not measurements: check:doc-formula-expressions, check:dts-closure, check:dual-build-cjs-loads, check:lean-entry-closure and check:sourcemap-no-sources-content. Under bash scripts/pm/os-verify-lock.sh with OS_VERIFY_LOCK_SLOT=os-dev-25169: turbo build of @objectstack/formula and @objectstack/lint gave 'VERDICT command-exit 0' (4 of 4 cached, FULL TURBO), then doc-formula-expressions exit 0. turbo run build --filter=!@objectstack/docs --concurrency=2 gave 'VERDICT command-exit 0', 76 of 76 tasks, held 323s. Then dts-closure exit 0 ('76 built package(s) swept - 179/179 declared declaration file(s) present'), dual-build-cjs-loads exit 0, lean-entry-closure exit 0 ('Admitted set held exactly (15 packages)') and sourcemap-no-sources-content exit 0 ('72 built package(s) swept - 598 map(s), none embed source text'). check:pm-skill-ratchet's last line: 'declared cross-file moves: 2, total ceilings down 486 lines'. --ran (dispatch-gates.mjs --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack --ran FILE, each family at its final reading): exit 0, 'Run reconciliation — 59 derived, 59 run, 0 NOT-MEASURED, 0 UNRUN', with rerun-failed --self-test recorded outside the derivation. node scripts/pm/check-governed-merges.mjs --pr 25186: exit 3 ('the given paths ARE governed'), 'GOVERNED — Tier S', 7 paths read from the PR's file list, 1 on the register (.claude/** x1, references/platform-readings.md), +1353/-55. git fetch origin main, then git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main HEAD against origin/main 2069b81c26: exit 0, a tree id alone (747bc3ac1a), no conflict. Main's five commits since the merge base touch none of the 7 paths, so no merge was made. CI check-runs on 49804f28cf, read once and not waited on: 41, all completed, 33 success and 8 skipped, none red. Required: Lint & Repo Gates=success; TypeScript Type Check=success; Test Core=success; Build Core=success (it ran this time); Governed Surface Queue Guard=success. Also Test Core 1/6 to 6/6, Type Check workspace, source gates, consumer gates and debt ledger, every Lint lane including PM dispatch-gates and scoped tooling self-tests, Validate Package Dependencies, Check PR Size, Check Documentation Links, Dogfood Regression Gate, Auto Label, filter and the four claim guards=success. Check Changeset=skipped: the synchronize payload already carries skip-changeset, the job's documented fast path. The rest were skipped: opt-in harnesses, Console Pin Gate, Temporal Conformance, Dogfood shards, Build Docs, Dogfood Verify CLI.",
