    {
      "body_line_at_f2ee5ad67d": 19,
      "replace": "The four run fences share one set of predicates, `RERUN_FAILED_FENCES` / `rerunFailedFenceFailures` in `ops.mjs`. The executor's `rerunFailedPreflight` reads attempt 1's job list first, as the read-back's baseline. It then reads `GET /repos/{repo}/actions/runs/{run_id}`, which is the last request before the POST, and judges the four fences on that answer. A run that changed between the request and the relay's run, for example one a person re-ran meanwhile, is refused there. A fence that fails, an unreadable run, an unreadable baseline or a baseline with no failed job stops the action with its POST row `not sent`: zero writes, exit 5, every failing fence named with what the run read. The wrapper judges the same four fences earlier and names the one that fails. That check is advisory and never replaces the executor's.",
      "with": "The five run fences share one set of predicates, `RERUN_FAILED_FENCES` / `rerunFailedFenceFailures` in `ops.mjs`; each takes the run and the pull's own answer. The executor's `rerunFailedPreflight` reads attempt 1's job list first, as the read-back's baseline. It then reads `GET /repos/{repo}/actions/runs/{run_id}` and, for the pull the run names, that pull's `GET /repos/{repo}/pulls/{n}`, the last two requests before the POST, and judges the five fences on those answers. A run that changed between the request and the relay's run, for example one a person re-ran meanwhile, or a pull pushed to meanwhile, is refused there. A fence that fails, an unreadable run or pull, an unreadable baseline or a baseline with no failed job stops the action with its POST row `not sent`: zero writes, exit 5, every failing fence named with what was read. The wrapper judges the same five fences earlier and names the one that fails. That check is advisory and never replaces the executor's."
    },
    {
      "body_line_at_f2ee5ad67d": 60,
      "replace": "The file's line budget is 120 bytes and its ceiling has zero headroom, so the line names the tool bare, as that file names every tool. It is paid for by deletion: it replaces the dated reading \"读数 2026-09-13:席位 REST `/jobs/{id}/rerun` 403、MCP `rerun_failed_jobs` 201 ⇒ 重跑可做,锁 1 未禁。\". The same REST 403 / MCP 201 reading stands at the file's earlier line, \"读数:`POST /actions/runs/{id}/rerun-failed-jobs` REST 回 403 而 MCP 回 201。\". `check:pm-skill-ratchet` stays green at 460 of 460 lines. `.claude/agents/os-dev.md` is not touched: a dev never re-runs.",
      "with": "The file's line budget is 120 bytes and its ceiling has zero headroom, so the line names the tool bare, as that file names every tool. It is paid for by deletion: it replaces the dated reading \"读数 2026-09-13:席位 REST `/jobs/{id}/rerun` 403、MCP `rerun_failed_jobs` 201 ⇒ 重跑可做,锁 1 未禁。\". The same REST 403 / MCP 201 reading stands at the file's earlier line, \"读数:`POST /actions/runs/{id}/rerun-failed-jobs` REST 回 403 而 MCP 回 201。\". `check:pm-skill-ratchet` stays green at 460 of 460 lines. `.claude/agents/os-dev.md` is not touched: a dev never re-runs. The head rule does not fit as well: the line measures 119 of its 120 bytes, so the `head` fence alone carries it, in code."
